cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below."
type: software
title: "CONFIGURE v1.1: Cost-benefit OptimisatioN Framework for Implementing blue-Green infrastructURE"
abstract: >-
  Python code that couples the NSGA-II multi-objective genetic algorithm with
  the CityCAT hydrodynamic flood model to optimise the location and combined
  size of Blue-Green Infrastructure, using direct damage cost and Expected
  Annual Damage over five rainstorm return periods.
version: 1.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Ur Rehman
    given-names: Asid
    affiliation: Newcastle University
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/asidurrehman/Configure11"
keywords:
  - NSGA-II
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - blue-green infrastructure
  - flood risk management
  - expected annual damage
  - CityCAT
